{"name":"Highland Winds","hex":"#d3dae3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high area; land that is higher than surrounding areas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highland"},{"term":"winds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wind"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of wind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Highland","blocks":[{"text":"Highlands or uplands are areas of high elevation such as a mountainous region, elevated mountainous plateau or high hills. Generally, upland refers to a range of hills, typically from 300 m (980 ft) up to 600 m (2,000 ft), while highland is usually reserved for ranges of low mountains. However, the two terms are interchangeable and also include regions that are transitional between hilly and mountainous terrain."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highland","wikidata":"Q878223"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind","wikidata":"Q8094"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg/500px-Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg/1280px-Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg/500px-Gleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glen Affric in the Scottish Highlands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGleann_Afraig_is_Beinn_Fhada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Puncakjaya.jpg/500px-Puncakjaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Puncakjaya.jpg/500px-Puncakjaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puncak Jaya is the highest mountain in Indonesia and Oceania","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuncakjaya.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/10_PM_March_12_surface_analysis_of_Great_Blizzard_of_1888.png/500px-10_PM_March_12_surface_analysis_of_Great_Blizzard_of_1888.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/10_PM_March_12_surface_analysis_of_Great_Blizzard_of_1888.png/500px-10_PM_March_12_surface_analysis_of_Great_Blizzard_of_1888.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Surface analysis of the Great Blizzard of 1888. Areas with greater isobaric packing indicate higher winds.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10_PM_March_12_surface_analysis_of_Great_Blizzard_of_1888.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Anemometer_2745.JPG/500px-Anemometer_2745.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1